Advanced machine learning (ML) algorithms, such as neural networks, tend to consume large amounts of data to make a prediction or classification. Moreover, these “black box” models make it difficult to derive exactly which data influenced the decision. This type of algorithm is becoming prevalent in many business-related activities, including business intelligence, marketing, and sales. It is therefore increasingly difficult to show adherence to the data minimization principle.
